<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat across Mediterranean ecosystems of Central Chile.">
  <title>Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat | Central Chile</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header class="mobile-header">
    <a class="brand" href="#home"><span class="brand-mark">gAT</span><span>Gradient of<br>Anthropogenic Threat</span></a>
    <button class="menu-toggle" id="menuToggle" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded="false">☰</button>
  </header>

  <main class="page-content">
    <section class="hero section" id="home">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> FONDECYT REGULAR PROJECT 1251095</div>
      <p class="hero-kicker">CENTRAL CHILE · MEDITERRANEAN ECOSYSTEMS</p>
      <h1>Understanding the<br><em>Gradient of</em><br>Anthropogenic Threat</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">An integrated spatial and field-based approach to characterize human pressure, biodiversity and locally observed threats across Mediterranean ecosystems of Central Chile.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-dark" href="#workflow">Explore the workflow <span>↘</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="#data">Explore repository data <span>→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note"><span class="status-dot"></span> Spatial indicators · Field assessment · Data integration</div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="hero-visual-label">STUDY LANDSCAPE <span>01 / CENTRAL CHILE</span></div>
        <div class="landscape-placeholder">
          <div class="placeholder-icon">＋</div>
          <strong>Landscape image placeholder</strong>
          <span>Add a representative photograph of Mediterranean ecosystems in Central Chile.</span>
          <small>Suggested file: <code>assets/central-chile-landscape.jpg</code></small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section intro-section" id="about">
      <div class="section-index">01 / ABOUT THE PROJECT</div>
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>A spatial perspective<br>on human pressure.</h2>
        <p>This project develops a spatial gradient of anthropogenic threat and evaluates how it relates to field-based biodiversity information and locally observed threats.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-grid">
        <article class="info-card"><span class="card-number">01</span><h3>Spatial pressure</h3><p>Three complementary spatial indicators are integrated to characterize anthropogenic pressure.</p></article>
        <article class="info-card"><span class="card-number">02</span><h3>Field evidence</h3><p>Vegetation structure and anonymous questionnaire responses contribute field-based information.</p></article>
        <article class="info-card"><span class="card-number">03</span><h3>Integration</h3><p>Spatial, biodiversity and locally observed threat information are brought together at the site level.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="indicators">
      <div class="section-index">02 / SPATIAL INDICATORS</div>
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Three indicators.<br><em>One spatial framework.</em></h2>
        <p>The gAT combines three normalized indicators aligned to a common 1-km grid and restricted to the study area.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="indicator-list">
        <article class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-meta"><span>INDICATOR 01</span><span class="tag">0—1 normalized</span></div>
          <div><h3>Road density</h3><p>Road density is calculated from the Chilean National Road Network using a 1-km grid and a 5 × 5 km moving window. Values are normalized using the 2nd and 98th percentiles.</p><small>Source: Dirección de Vialidad, MOP (2024)</small></div>
          <div class="visual-slot"><div class="slot-top">MAP / RASTER PLACEHOLDER <span>01</span></div><div class="map-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert road density map</b><small>Replace with the processed Road_density.tif visualization.</small></div></div>
        </article>
        <article class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-meta"><span>INDICATOR 02</span><span class="tag">0—1 normalized</span></div>
          <div><h3>Loss of natural ecosystems</h3><p>Identifies pixels classified as natural in 2000 that transitioned to anthropogenic land-cover classes by 2024. The proportion of converted natural land is aggregated to approximately 1-km resolution.</p><small>Source: MapBiomas Chile, Collection 2 (2025)</small></div>
          <div class="visual-slot"><div class="slot-top">MAP / RASTER PLACEHOLDER <span>02</span></div><div class="map-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert ecosystem loss map</b><small>Replace with the processed Loss_Nature.tif visualization.</small></div></div>
        </article>
        <article class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-meta"><span>INDICATOR 03</span><span class="tag">0—1 continuous</span></div>
          <div><h3>Global Human Modification</h3><p>The Global Human Modification dataset is processed and aligned to the common 1-km spatial grid while retaining its continuous 0–1 representation.</p><small>Source: Kennedy et al. (2019)</small></div>
          <div class="visual-slot"><div class="slot-top">MAP / RASTER PLACEHOLDER <span>03</span></div><div class="map-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert GHM map</b><small>Replace with the processed GHM.tif visualization.</small></div></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section gradient-section" id="gat">
      <div class="section-index">03 / THE GRADIENT</div>
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>From indicators<br>to a <em>continuous gradient.</em></h2>
        <p>The Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat (gAT) is calculated as the arithmetic mean of the three normalized spatial indicators.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-panel">
        <div class="formula-label">gAT FORMULA</div>
        <div class="formula">gAT = <span>(RD + LNE + GHM)</span> / 3</div>
        <div class="formula-key"><span>RD · Road density</span><span>LNE · Loss of natural ecosystems</span><span>GHM · Global Human Modification</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="map-feature">
        <div class="feature-copy"><span class="mini-label">MAIN SPATIAL OUTPUT</span><h3>The Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat</h3><p>Urban areas and a 1-km surrounding buffer are excluded from the study domain. The continuous gradient is subsequently classified into five empirical quintiles.</p><div class="quintile-key"><span><i></i> Q1 · Lowest</span><span><i></i> Q2</span><span><i></i> Q3</span><span><i></i> Q4</span><span><i></i> Q5 · Highest</span></div></div>
        <div class="large-map-placeholder"><div class="slot-top">FINAL gAT MAP <span>04</span></div><div class="map-placeholder map-large"><span>＋</span><b>Insert final gAT map</b><small>Replace with gAT.tif or gAT_quintiles.tif.</small></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="field">
      <div class="section-index">04 / FIELD ASSESSMENT</div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Connecting spatial patterns<br>with <em>field evidence.</em></h2><p>Candidate sites distributed along the spatial gradient were evaluated using two complementary sources of field information.</p></div>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <article class="field-card"><div class="field-card-head"><span>FIELD COMPONENT 01</span><span class="field-symbol">✳</span></div><h3>Woody plant biodiversity</h3><p>Vegetation structure data are used to characterize woody plant diversity at each site. The workflow considers woody individuals with DBH ≥ 3 cm.</p><div class="metric-chips"><span>Hill q = 0</span><span>Hill q = 1</span><span>Hill q = 2</span></div><div class="chart-slot"><div class="slot-top">CHART PLACEHOLDER <span>05</span></div><div class="chart-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert biodiversity chart</b><small>For example: Hill diversity by site or gAT quintile.</small></div></div></article>
        <article class="field-card"><div class="field-card-head"><span>FIELD COMPONENT 02</span><span class="field-symbol">⌁</span></div><h3>Locally observed threats</h3><p>Anonymized questionnaires characterize locally observed anthropogenic threats. Threat extent, severity and temporal status are standardized to a common 0–1 scale.</p><div class="metric-chips"><span>Extent</span><span>Severity</span><span>Temporal status</span></div><div class="chart-slot"><div class="slot-top">CHART PLACEHOLDER <span>06</span></div><div class="chart-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert questionnaire chart</b><small>For example: threat categories by site.</small></div></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section integration-section" id="integration">
      <div class="section-index">05 / FINAL INTEGRATION</div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Bringing multiple dimensions<br><em>together.</em></h2><p>The final analysis integrates spatial threat, locally observed anthropogenic threats, biodiversity metrics and native-species composition.</p></div>
      <div class="integration-diagram">
        <div class="integration-inputs"><div class="integration-node"><span>01</span><b>Spatial gAT</b><small>Continuous gradient</small></div><div class="integration-node"><span>02</span><b>Local threats</b><small>Questionnaire assessment</small></div><div class="integration-node"><span>03</span><b>Biodiversity</b><small>Hill diversity metrics</small></div><div class="integration-node"><span>04</span><b>Native composition</b><small>Species composition</small></div></div>
        <div class="integration-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="integration-output"><span>FINAL INTEGRATIVE ANALYSIS</span><h3>Correspondence & candidate site selection</h3><p>Evaluation of correspondence among spatial, field-based and biodiversity indicators, and comparison of alternative combinations of candidate sites.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-slot integration-chart"><div class="slot-top">RESULTS / FIGURE PLACEHOLDER <span>07</span></div><div class="chart-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Insert final integration figure</b><small>Add the final plots, ordinations, comparisons or tables when available.</small></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="sites">
      <div class="section-index">06 / STUDY SITES</div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Where the gradient<br>meets the <em>landscape.</em></h2><p>Candidate sites are distributed along the spatial gradient and assessed using field information.</p></div>
      <div class="site-layout"><div class="site-map-placeholder"><span>＋</span><b>Study sites map placeholder</b><small>Add parcels_fieldcheck.gpkg or a map showing candidate and visited plots.</small></div><div class="site-notes"><div><b>Spatial coverage</b><p>Map the study area and the distribution of field-assessment plots.</p></div><div><b>Site information</b><p>Add site labels, gAT quintile, field status and relevant site-level summaries when available.</p></div><div><b>Field records</b><p>Use the visited-plots dataset to document field assessment coverage.</p></div></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section data-section" id="data">
      <div class="section-index">07 / DATA & REPRODUCIBILITY</div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Explore the <em>repository.</em></h2><p>Data and R scripts document the analytical workflow from spatial indicator construction to final integration.</p></div>
      <div class="repo-list">
        <div class="repo-row"><span class="repo-number">01</span><div><b>Spatial data</b><small>Processed raster and vector products</small></div><code>01_spatial/</code></div>
        <div class="repo-row"><span class="repo-number">02</span><div><b>Field data</b><small>Vegetation structure and field plot information</small></div><code>02_field/</code></div>
        <div class="repo-row"><span class="repo-number">03</span><div><b>Questionnaire</b><small>Anonymized field threat assessments</small></div><code>03_questionnaire/</code></div>
        <div class="repo-row"><span class="repo-number">04</span><div><b>Integrated data</b><small>Site-level input for final integration</small></div><code>04_integrated_data/</code></div>
        <div class="repo-row"><span class="repo-number">05</span><div><b>R scripts</b><small>Seven scripts documenting the workflow</small></div><code>05_Scripts/</code></div>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-dark repo-button" href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Add your repository URL <span>↗</span></a>
      <p class="repo-hint">Update the repository link in <code>index.html</code> when the public GitHub URL is ready.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section references-section" id="references">
      <div class="section-index">08 / REFERENCES</div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Data sources &<br><em>references.</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="references-list">
        <li>Kennedy, C. M., Oakleaf, J. R., Theobald, D. M., Baruch-Mordo, S., & Kiesecker, J. (2019). Managing the middle: A shift in conservation priorities based on the global human modification gradient. <i>Global Change Biology, 25</i>(3), 811–826.</li>
        <li>MapBiomas Chile Project. (2025). <i>Collection 2 of the Annual Series of Land Cover and Land Use Maps of Chile (1999–2024).</i> Accessed through Google Earth Engine.</li>
        <li>Dirección de Vialidad, Ministerio de Obras Públicas (MOP). (2024). <i>Red Vial Nacional de Chile.</i> Dataset version dated 7 February 2024.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <footer class="footer"><span class="brand-mark">gAT</span><span>Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat · Central Chile</span><a href="#home">Back to top ↑</a></footer>
  </main>

